WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.238
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.238 --> 00:00:14.799
Today, skills: what your characters are actually good at, and how they get better at it.

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.996
Open Mechanics, then Skills.

6
00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:23.257
Voyage starts you with seven, and I've added three for our circus: knife throwing,

7
00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:25.631
sleight of hand, and animal handling.

8
00:00:25.631 --> 00:00:27.299
Let's open knife throwing.

9
00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:32.473
The description is the main thing the AI reads when the skill gets used.

10
00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:37.264
Say what it covers, then what a poor roll, a good roll and a great roll look like.

11
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:44.964
Type. Combat is special: a combat skill adds a point of damage for every two points of its attribute above six.

12
00:00:44.964 --> 00:00:47.975
No other type does that, so this one's combat.

13
00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:52.758
Attribute is the stat that adds to this skill's checks.

14
00:00:52.758 --> 00:00:55.353
Knife throwing runs on dexterity.

15
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.088
And starting items are handed over with the skill,

16
00:00:59.088 --> 00:01:02.640
whether a character starts with it or learns it later.

17
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.994
Knife throwing comes with a set of throwing knives.

18
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.308
Now Skill Settings, under Skills.

19
00:01:09.308 --> 00:01:12.778
This switch lets Voyage invent brand new skills during play.

20
00:01:12.778 --> 00:01:16.421
Turn it off and characters only ever have the skills you wrote.

21
00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:22.507
Skill type difficulty bonus adds a flat bonus to every check made with a skill of that type.

22
00:01:22.507 --> 00:01:27.350
They're all zero here, so the type is just a label, apart from combat's damage.

23
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:33.713
When someone tries a skill they don't have, there's a chance they learn it: a one in ten base chance,

24
00:01:33.713 --> 00:01:36.933
plus a little for every point of the skill's attribute.

25
00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:41.616
Set both of these to zero and nobody learns new skills after character creation.

26
00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.982
And skills level through use.

27
00:01:43.982 --> 00:01:46.757
The first level takes a hundred skill X P,

28
00:01:46.757 --> 00:01:50.588
and every level after that takes forty more than the last.

29
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.724
One tip from Voyage's own docs: don't make a pile of skills that all do the same thing.

30
00:01:57.724 --> 00:02:03.711
Skills level up through use, so overlapping skills split the X P and all of them stay weak.

31
00:02:03.711 --> 00:02:09.171
And spread your skills across different attributes, so no one stat does everything.

32
00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:11.567
That's skills.

33
00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:13.859
Our three are linked in the description.

34
00:02:13.859 --> 00:02:18.903
Next time, resources: health, stamina, and anything else your characters can run out of.

35
00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:23.315
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

